@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About BasketElo</PageTitle>

<div class="info-page about-page">
    <header class="info-hero be-reveal" style="--reveal-order: 0">
        <div class="info-hero-copy">
            <p class="info-kicker">About</p>
            <h1>A basketball question I wanted to answer.</h1>
            <p class="info-lede">I had always found ELO interesting. I had seen it used in chess and football, but I could not find a basketball version that let me explore the leagues and comparisons I cared about. So I started building one.</p>
        </div>
        <dl class="info-facts" aria-label="About the project">
            <div><dt>What it is</dt><dd>A personal project</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Why it exists</dt><dd>Curiosity</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>Still evolving</dd></div>
        </dl>
    </header>

    <section class="info-section be-reveal" style="--reveal-order: 1" aria-labelledby="beginning-heading">
        <div class="info-section-label"><span>01</span><span>The beginning</span></div>
        <div class="info-section-body about-prose">
            <h2 id="beginning-heading">It began as a spare-time experiment.</h2>
            <p>I wanted to put teams from different European leagues on the same rating map and see what the results said. The idea was small: collect the games, run ELO, and publish a ranking.</p>
            <p>I am an engineer, but I did not have the time to build a project of this size in the usual way. The arrival of capable AI tools changed that. They made it possible to turn short pockets of spare time into a working application and keep following the questions as they grew.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="info-section be-reveal" style="--reveal-order: 2" aria-labelledby="journey-heading">
        <div class="info-section-label"><span>02</span><span>The journey</span></div>
        <div class="info-section-body">
            <h2 id="journey-heading">The formula was the easy part.</h2>
            <p class="info-section-intro">Once the first data arrived, the project became less about one equation and more about making basketball history understandable.</p>
            <ol class="about-journey">
                <li><span>First</span><div><h3>A ranking</h3><p>The first goal was simply to compare European clubs using a transparent ELO model.</p></div></li>
                <li><span>Then</span><div><h3>The data fought back</h3><p>Archives disagreed, clubs changed names, competitions changed shape, and a source ID was not always a real team identity.</p></div></li>
                <li><span>Next</span><div><h3>The questions expanded</h3><p>The NBA and national teams joined the project, along with team histories, game explanations, and tools for testing different models.</p></div></li>
                <li><span>Now</span><div><h3>An ongoing investigation</h3><p>Coverage is improving, assumptions remain visible, and a better source or method can change what the site knows.</p></div></li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="info-section be-reveal" style="--reveal-order: 3" aria-labelledby="ai-heading">
        <div class="info-section-label"><span>03</span><span>Built with AI</span></div>
        <div class="info-section-body about-prose">
            <h2 id="ai-heading">AI made the project possible. Evidence keeps it honest.</h2>
            <p>BasketElo has been developed through conversations with AI: shaping features, writing code, tracing bugs, testing imports, and documenting decisions. That speed is what allowed a hobby idea to become a real product.</p>
            <p>It also makes provenance, tests, versioned models, and visible warnings especially important. The aim is not to sound certain. It is to show what the ratings use, where the games came from, and where the data still has limits.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <aside class="about-closing be-reveal" style="--reveal-order: 4">
        <div>
            <span>Why continue?</span>
            <strong>Because I am still curious what the next result will change.</strong>
        </div>
        <nav aria-label="Continue exploring">
            <a href="rankings">Explore the rankings <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
            <a href="how-it-works">Read the method <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </nav>
    </aside>
</div>
